{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773938840,"nonce":"4Sq17IKbwFhat82dIX9JGDMz0dY=","title":"SDK console sessions stuck at \"Starting…\" / \"Waiting for reply\"","message":"Three interlocking bugs cause SDK console sessions to appear permanently stuck:\n\n**Bug 1 — Stale-event overwrite in hydration fallback (main cause)**\nWhen `provider_session_id` is first set (event [0] fires), the TerminalPane hydration effect re-runs. At that moment only 0–2 events are in the event log (no `assistant` event yet — that arrives at index 13 of 19). `hasRenderableEvents` returns false, so the effect falls through to the async conversation-history fetch path. While `getConversations` is in-flight, real-time SSE events accumulate in `streamEvents` via `handleStreamEvent`. When the fetch resolves (conversation not indexed yet), it calls `setStreamEvents(events)` using a STALE LOCAL VARIABLE from the closure — the 0–2 partial events from before the fetch — overwriting everything the SSE handler accumulated.\n\nFix: in the \"no conversation found\" branch, do NOT call `setStreamEvents(events)`. Just call `setStreaming(false)`. The hydration path for \"no conversation\" should only clear streaming, never clobber SSE state.\n\n**Bug 2 — `streaming` stuck true when SSE miss during reconnect**\nIf the SSE connection drops at the moment `console:session:updated` (carrying `provider_session_id`) fires (e.g. daemon rebuild mid-stream), the browser never receives that event, `providerSessionId` stays null in the React state, and the hydration effect (deps: `[providerSessionId, sessionId]`) never re-runs with the completed events. Meanwhile `streaming=true` (set optimistically on submit) is never cleared. The session stays visually stuck indefinitely.\n\nFix: add a polling fallback in TerminalPane — if `streaming===true` for \u003e15 s, re-fetch stream events; if the last event is `result`, materialise everything and clear streaming.\n\n**Bug 3 — Session status stays \"running\" forever after SDK completes**\n`processPromptQueue` sets `this.processing = false` when the queue drains, but never calls `stop()` or emits a status change. The session remains in `\"running\"` status in the DB and in SSE broadcasts after the result event fires.\n\nFix: after `processPromptQueue` drains the queue, emit status `\"stopped\"` via `emitMetaUpdate` + `emitStatus`.\n\nObserved: session af476039 processed 19 events (incl. `assistant` at idx 13, `result:success` at idx 18) hours ago; status still shows `\"running\"` in the API.","files":null}]}